  "title": "Will the real trusted advisor please stand up?",
  "summary": "I’ve been in business development my entire career, and I’m passionate about sales ethics and meeting my clients' expectations. Recently, I’ve been engaged in conversations about what it means to be a “trusted advisor.” A trusted advisor used to mean something specific; now it seems everyone claims to be one. Yet being a trusted advisor—or trusted partner—isn’t something you can just claim. It must be earned.",
